## Hermes agent temp & analysis cache
.hermes-tmp.*/
.hermes/

## Research references and mirrored reference repos, anchored to the root on purpose: unanchored,
## these two rules swallowed skills/ocoreai/references/ — the three files SKILL.md cites by name, so
## the published skill shipped dangling pointers that every on-disk check saw as resolved. Probe 39
## §0 asks git for that reason.
/reference/
/references/
# `docs/` was added here for a mirrored reference tree, and it silently swallowed the
# project's own evidence layer: AGENTS.md routes its long-form proof into docs/agent/*.md,
# `make docs-check` budgets those guides, and `make anchor-check` verifies cites inside
# them — none of which exists in a fresh clone while the directory is ignored. Keep
# mirroring out, keep the routing targets in.
docs/*
!docs/agent/
!docs/agent/**
.status.md

# Local scrapling venv (tooling, not project code)
.scrapling_venv/

# swift test profile dumps
default.profraw

# local quarantine: model-test artifacts, backups (kept out of git status noise)
.untracked-quarantine/
dist/

# CLT-route scratch path (make test-clt)
.build-clt/
.build-ios/
.build-*/
tmp/

# agent sandbox scratch (clang module caches) — never a source of truth
.codex-tmp/

# live-probe run logs: written next to the tree by scripts/probes/, uploaded by CI on failure
probe-*.log
probe41.log
serve_smoke.log
serve_health.json
